<title>SINGAPORE: Australia's Ampol restarts 22,000-bpd cracker.</title>
<headline>Australia's Ampol restarts 22,000-bpd cracker.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Petroleum Pty Ltd (Ampol) restarted its 22,000 barrel-per-day fluid catalytic cracker (FCC) at Kurnell February 2 after a near month-long unscheduled shutdown, a company source said on Monday.</p>
<p>Regenerator problems on January 7 had forced the country's largest refiner to first cut runs at the FCC and then shut it down.</p>
<p>The source said throughput at the 115,000-bpd refinery were under review amid low middle distillate margins.</p>
<p>&quot;But it's is nothing we will rush into,&quot; the source said.  </p>
<p>Ampol is jointly owned by Pioneer International Ltd and Caltex Australia Ltd.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
